And it was just, it was
sad to see how

00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:13.583
the media, again,
they didn't allow themselves

00:09:13.583 --> 00:09:16.625
an opportunity to know
who we are as people

00:09:16.625 --> 00:09:18.750
and they went
into the perception

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.000
of who they thought we were

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.625
and again, we
just went out there

00:09:21.625 --> 00:09:23.417
and we just had fun
with the game.

00:09:23.417 --> 00:09:25.458
- It makes it more interesting
to have the villains

00:09:25.458 --> 00:09:27.333
to have someone to talk about.
There has to be a bad guy.

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:31.125
- There has to be.
- They have to, but it's unfair, like you said

00:09:31.125 --> 00:09:35.833
because, again, how can you
justify Tom Brady doin'

00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:38.958
or sayin' some of the same
things that I've done—

00:09:38.958 --> 00:09:40.625
- Right.
- Showing emotion.

00:09:40.625 --> 00:09:42.292
- Right, yelling the
F-word at the stands.

00:09:42.292 --> 00:09:44.500
- Right. Exactly.
I've seen him curse out coaches.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.792
I've seen him berate his own teammates.
- Yeah, right.

00:09:46.792 --> 00:09:51.542
- But he's looked at and upon as
a leader, a champion, you know?

00:09:51.542 --> 00:09:54.125
- You know what,
if I had to do it again

00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:56.042
honestly, to restart
and had to do it again

00:09:56.042 --> 00:09:58.375
I'd do it the exact same way.

00:09:58.375 --> 00:09:59.875
I wouldn't change s--t.

00:10:01.125 --> 00:10:03.583
- So T.O. just surprised us.
- Right.

00:10:03.583 --> 00:10:06.000
- Like, we were hangin' out with
Chad Johnson, in comes T.O.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.583
Those two are
really like brothers.

00:10:07.583 --> 00:10:09.417
- Oh, I thought he came
because he was like

00:10:09.417 --> 00:10:11.333
"Damn, Simms is there.
Let me go hang out with him."

00:10:11.333 --> 00:10:12.833
I'm pretty sure
that's why he came by.

00:10:12.833 --> 00:10:14.000
- You think so?
- I think so.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.458
I'm pretty cool.
- That's great.

00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:17.417
Well, see, that's the truth
he believes

00:10:17.417 --> 00:10:19.583
but what he's saying,
it's not really honest.

00:10:19.583 --> 00:10:22.042
And sometimes we hear
coaches talk, and we go

00:10:22.042 --> 00:10:23.542
"That's not the truth."

00:10:23.542 --> 00:10:26.500
So it's time for a little bit
of "Coach Speak."

00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:30.417
All right, Simms, first one,
you're doin' it.

00:10:30.417 --> 00:10:32.750
Marrone comes out and says,
"I did it to try

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.208
and get a spark from this team
to put everyone on notice."

00:10:35.208 --> 00:10:36.875
That's the reason
he benched Bortles.

00:10:36.875 --> 00:10:38.167
- Right.
- What's the truth?

00:10:38.167 --> 00:10:39.875
- The truth is:
"Ha ha ha ha!

00:10:39.875 --> 00:10:43.333
The old 'spark the team by
benching the quarterback' trick.

00:10:43.333 --> 00:10:45.125
Uh, think they bought that one?

00:10:45.125 --> 00:10:47.375
I mean, come on. You guys
are watchin' the game.

00:10:47.375 --> 00:10:49.083
This guy can't throw
the football.

00:10:49.083 --> 00:10:51.708
What am I supposed to do?
No wonder nobody wanted this job

00:10:51.708 --> 00:10:53.167
when they first tried
to hire me."

00:10:53.167 --> 00:10:55.000
- All right, so,
Vrabel went for two

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.292
at the end of the game
against the Chargers.
- Yup.

00:10:57.292 --> 00:10:59.333
- And after the game,
he said, you know

00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:01.333
"We put a lot of faith
into our players.

00:11:01.333 --> 00:11:04.250
Face the same situation, I'd like
to think I'd do it the same way."

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:06.083
What he really wanted
to say is

00:11:06.083 --> 00:11:07.667
"Hey, guys, here's the truth.

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:09.917
I'm a linebacker,
and I think like a linebacker.

00:11:09.917 --> 00:11:12.958
I put two fingers in the air
and I say, 'Get me the win.'

00:11:12.958 --> 00:11:16.667
Did I want a slant
from Mariota at the 1?

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:19.833
No. My OC, what are you doin'?!

00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:22.125
You got a mobile quarterback
and Derrick Henry.

00:11:22.125 --> 00:11:23.542
Figure it out!"

00:11:23.542 --> 00:11:24.917
All right, Vrabel.

00:11:24.917 --> 00:11:26.750
- Doug Pederson,
my coach of my Eagles—

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.917
man, he looks teary-eyed
in that photo—

00:11:28.917 --> 00:11:30.417
sayin', "Pressure's off, man.

00:11:30.417 --> 00:11:33.833
We can go and play and have fun
and just relax."

00:11:33.833 --> 00:11:35.792
But what he's really
thinking is

00:11:35.792 --> 00:11:38.917
"Ahhh!
What the hell is goin' on?!

00:11:38.917 --> 00:11:41.667
We won the Super Bowl, and now
I'm losing control of everything

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.542
and Carson Wentz
can't do it all by himself

00:11:43.542 --> 00:11:45.917
and my defense is falling apart!
What the f--k?!"

00:11:45.917 --> 00:11:48.542
So that took a lot out of me.
- Oh, it should've.

00:11:48.542 --> 00:11:50.792
- That one was a little personal.
- I liked it.

00:11:50.792 --> 00:11:54.125
- So, last week, we said that
